story\">As of Oct 12, the record from 1951 to 2025 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids shows January to February and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, March to April ran 242% of normal and September to October ran 42%. Grid 18430 had its driest year in 1954 at 51%. The preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 on grid 17832 sits at 21.9, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
